  hintId: tutorial_training_4
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Decision Making
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'So far, you have learned how to read values using <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#55FF55>scan</color>()</font> and <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#55FF55>measure</color>()</font>.
    But in real situations, there can be multiple outcomes that require different
    actions.


    Decision making allows the robot to choose what to do based on
    conditions in the environment. Instead of always following the same instructions,
    the robot can react differently depending on what it detects.


    In this level,
    you will decide what to do based on whether the tile in front is a white ore.
    Decision making is what allows programs to behave intelligently instead of running
    in a fixed sequence.'
  isImageBig: 0
